{
  "requirement": "The SDK derives the submission tool's JSON schema from `R` using `schemars`\nand instructs the agent to finish through that tool. Its default name is\n`submit_result`; harness configuration can preserve an application's existing\nnames and acceptance rules.\n\nA successful call returns exactly one accepted submitted value, deserialized\ninto `R`. Ordinary assistant text does not count. Ending without a valid\naccepted submission returns an error. Provider failures and invalid terminal\nsubmissions return `ValidationError::Agent`, rather than a node judgment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.submission` that has a MUST or SHOULD force.\n\n**Schema derived from `R` and the default name.**\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` asserts that the provider request has a tool named `submit_result`. It also asserts that the schema for `bool` has `properties.result.type == \"boolean\"`.\n- `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors` checks a derived type. It asserts that `$defs.Decision` exists and that `properties.result.properties.decision.$ref` points to it.\n- The `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` test in `validation.rs` asserts the integer schema that reaches the agent.\n\n**Instructing the agent to finish through the tool.** `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts that the opening request contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\".\n\n**A successful call returns one accepted value, deserialized into `R`.**\n- The `bool` scenario in `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` returns the submitted value.\n- The `Answer` scenario with `Decision::Yes` returns the deserialized struct.\n- The `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` test returns `answer.n == 7`.\n- `unknown_tools_return_errors_without_creating_inputs_or_preventing_submission` shows that an unknown tool call does not prevent a later valid submission. It returns true.\n\n**Failure cases, all returning `ValidationError::Agent`.**\n- A wrong-typed result, two `submit_result` calls in one turn (so not exactly one), and an extra top-level field each produce `Err(ValidationError::Agent(_))`. These are the three scenarios in `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors`.\n- `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error` covers an invalid typed submission through a separate mock agent.\n- Assistant text only is not a result. `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts the error text \"without invoking submit_result\". It also asserts that the provider was called twice, so ending without a submission is checked.\n- A provider failure produces `ValidationError::Agent` with \"permanent provider failure\". No dependencies are recorded.\n\n**Not tested: configurable names and acceptance rules.** The text says \"harness configuration can preserve an application's existing names and acceptance rules\". That is a statement of capability, not a MUST or SHOULD, so I did not treat it as an obligation that needs a test. The only generic `converse` test uses the default name, and I found no SDK test of a custom name. The `ReviewAgent` implementation in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` uses its own names, but that is application configuration.\n\nI found no gap in the MUST-level behavior, so the tests adequately check the requirement.",
  "references": "aa9da1e031d3261338e28ef37780123a1edfa58000bfdb8e811732db4347d5d9",
